      "id": "claim_15905714cd7a4819b90d8896103513b9",
      "statement": "Resident-cell count is deliberately NOT pressure-managed: it is a hard cap enforced at admission (self-limiting and known exactly), while the pressure classifier answers only 'is this node out of memory and must give cells back to recover?' — conflating the two produced placement churn and an admission wedge, so splitting them keeps each decision small.",
      "evidence": [
