      "id": "claim_bf3825c690fa4fb19af6c0d14cc6b312",
      "statement": "One sampling turn (memory::sample) returns an intact relationship: rss_bytes, in_use_bytes (RSS minus allocator slack), cgroup_working_set_bytes, and cgroup_current_bytes; the Linux cgroup read covers v2 (/sys/fs/cgroup/memory.current + memory.stat's inactive_file) and v1 (/sys/fs/cgroup/memory/memory.usage_in_bytes + total_inactive_file) layouts; non-Linux has no cgroup measurement.",
