    {
      "id": "claim_205be14f832b43e7898406f921e523c8",
      "statement": "The pressure config carries two watermarks without residency: high_bytes (CELLD_MAX_RSS_MB sets it; applies to allocator-adjusted RSS and cgroup working set so a node recovers after a free) and an absolute cap at 95% of available memory (or process RSS without a readable cgroup) that protects kernel charges RSS cannot see — a fixed share of the machine never derived from high_bytes; an earlier 'at least 125% of the ceiling' placement pushed it above anything the kernel allows and was corrected.",
      "evidence": [
