    {
      "id": "claim_babfd64cd41a42a892216b2c475ea638",
      "statement": "Documented memory-pressure behavior: default threshold 80% of available memory (CELLD_MAX_RSS_MB to change, 0 disables threshold and cap), computed as the greater of allocator-adjusted RSS and the active cgroup working set (memory.current minus inactive_file then minus allocator slack, including active kernel charges and excluding pages shedding cannot return); a separate cap applies at 95% (from process RSS without a cgroup) with logged warnings; shedding releases at 80% of its threshold value and the cap releases at 80% of its own, so hysteresis keeps a crossing from holding the other limit.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L267-L311",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:664c33814a3c5cf3957d2b463435d6c50df94fa98054446aaddcc5994b3af1dd:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fc9adaa782144bfeaa80d1c51113eec9",
      "statement": "Under pressure celld durably replicates and fences the least-recently used idle cells, publishes them as unowned without resetting their epochs, and refuses to reacquire new unowned cells; it never sheds a cell with active work or a live host WebSocket; a spare node acquires the released cells via the same bucket protocol rather than preemptive assignment.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L288-L296",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:79c7c87715e9faf918a6732f102f7dd36c91bacadac0a6565375da38ec12e782:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3d83a00c82b24a12897d5e1486bf8c47",
      "statement": "Per-cell request admission: at most 64 concurrent fetch events for one Durable Object or Queue broker (CELLD_MAX_CELL_REQUESTS); the excess event returns HTTP 503 without starting, with Retry-After: 1 and X-Celld-Overload: cell, and Queue producer admission refusal has body {\"error\":\"cell admission refused\"} and must be counted by fixed-rate clients as rejected work so a retry does not inflate the offered rate; the cell_overload_refused event (scope, node, region, in-flight, limit) is counted separately from transport errors and application failures.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L640-L655",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6bdc381b7f687feb8276d762a610aa69b4304195d858ee31a384a02aa4f7d3e0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b4777dc8b6fc40419ab0bcc30c71563d",
      "statement": "Per-isolate V8 heap limit (default 128 MB matching Cloudflare Durable Objects, CELD_V8_HEAP_LIMIT_MB) governs hibernatable WebSocket capacity (~50k clients at 128MB, ~512MB for 100k); above 90% an isolate refuses new hibernatable WebSockets, at the limit it stops SQL result-set materialization, celld re-measures before each event and re-serves under 75%, forcing collection above that share on an idle isolate so no restart is needed.",
